---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About & methodology — Actual Play Database"
  description="How credits are sourced, tiered, and corroborated on the Actual Play Database."
>
  <h1>About & methodology</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Community-curated. Every entry is a file in git; every correction is a
    pull request.
  </p>

  <h2>Source tiers</h2>
  <p>
    Every credit is tagged with its source tier, ranked by how close the
    source was to the thing happening:
    <span class="tag tier tier--strong">official</span>
    <span class="tag tier tier--strong">recording</span>
    <span class="tag tier tier--strong">participant</span>
    <span class="tag tier tier--medium">saw it firsthand</span>
    <span class="tag tier tier--medium">reference work</span>
    <span class="tag tier tier--medium">community</span>.
  </p>

  <h2>Corroboration</h2>
  <p>
    A credit shows <span class="tag tag--corroborated">corroborated</span>
    once two independent sources agree, and
    <span class="tag tag--flag">single source</span> until then — a second
    person who watched the same episode is enough, no publisher required.
    Where nobody established which name was on the billing, we say so
    rather than guess.
  </p>
  <p>
    Someone who watched the episode outranks a published summary of it —
    they were closer to the fact. Unlike Wikipedia, we admit unpublished
    firsthand accounts, because for much of the indie long tail a listener
    is the only source that will ever exist. Whether a stranger can go and
    check is a separate question, marked
    <span class="tag tag--flag">uncorroborated</span>.
  </p>
</Base>
